All figures are saved in JPG format at 300 dpi.

## Interpretation and Limitations

This analysis is designed to evaluate mutation detection consistency between sequencing lanes of the same MA line. Shared mutations are counted once in feature-level summaries, and statistical comparisons focus on replicate-specific mutations.

Differences in genomic features may reflect sequencing coverage, mapping quality, variant-calling sensitivity, or filtering rather than biological differences. The analyses do not directly estimate mutation rates or establish causal sequencing-lane effects.

Additional analyses incorporating read depth, alternate allele counts, variant allele fractions, and callable genomic regions are recommended for a more comprehensive evaluation of sequencing reproducibility.
